{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>For not like our Rock, etc.</b> The meaning is: the reason they would advance — for their rock sold them and HaShem delivered them — and they would not say it out of denying the power of HaShem, etc., heaven forbid; as Moses said to HaShem in the incident of the spies. For the strength of Israel is not like the strength of the nations, for there is no idolatry that endured many days, in the secret of (Proverbs 12:19) ״וְעַד אַרְגִּיעָה לְשׁוֹן שָׁקֶר״ — and go out and learn from the idolatry of Chemosh, after which the majority of the nations strayed, and how many wonders it performed, as written in the words of our master Saadiah Gaon — yet even so it became as though it had never been, and many like these. But our Rock, whose power is exalted, ascends in holiness, and even the nations will agree to this, as stated in the words of the prophet (Malachi 1:11) ״כִּי גָדוֹל שְׁמִי בַּגּוֹיִם״. And when they see the catastrophe of Israel in this manner, they too will judge the same, and this is what the verse says ״וְאֹיְבֵינוּ פְּלִילִים״ — the language of judges, as stated (Exodus 21:22) ״וְנָתַן בִּפְלִילִים״ — meaning, they too will judge that their rock is not like our Rock; rather, when they see the destruction of Israel they will recognize the truth, as written ״פֶּן יְנַכְּרוּ וְגוֹ׳ פֶּן יֹאמְרוּ״ וְגוֹ׳."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The abbreviated quotation ״פֶּן יְנַכְּרוּ וְגוֹ׳ פֶּן יֹאמְרוּ״ וְגוֹ׳ alludes to Deuteronomy 32:26–27, left as an elliptical citation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:37.812945469Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}